<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ley Juárez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ley Juárez was a Mexican law of November 1855, drafted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-juarez">Benito Juárez</a> as minister of justice, that abolished the special courts of the clergy and the military for civil cases. Part of the liberal programme of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-reforma">La Reforma</a>, it was the first of the reform laws that limited the corporate privileges of the Church and army. Its passage provoked conservative revolts, and its principles were confirmed by the Constitution of 1857.</p></div>
